# Create Multi Command

A multi command is a named sequence of smaller commands.

## Use when

A feature needs one user action to trigger several existing commands in a known order.

## Good case

Compose existing commands into an ordered chain.

## Bad case

Using a multi command as a giant dumping ground for everything.

## Key API

- extend the multi command base and declare the chain of command classes to run in order.
- pass shared data through the wave or a `WaveBean`.

Template: `templates/MultiCommandTemplate.java.txt`.
